{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions","id":1011140,"title":"Changing a few merits into positive conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T10:59:57-08:00","id":1011140,"title":"Changing a few merits into positive conditions","content":"Namely:<br /> - Retainer<br /> - Contact<br /> - Allies<br /> - Resource<br /> - Mentor<br /> - Status<br /> <br /> It occurred to me that the way i was using those merits fell more in line with conditions than the way they are written. By that i mean that if the player do something that would logically earn them the merit I don't bother with the exp spending. Also i've not been following the mechanics of these merits too closely, a player tells me what they want to accomplish and i judge if its feasible with the merits they have.<br /> I also really like the ... flowing nature of how conditions work, the way you gain and lose them. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of awarding the condition following appropriate story circumstances (same as any other condition). I'd also add something i call 'strings attached' which is what the players need to do in order to keep the condition. <br /> You earn beats for gaining or losing the condition.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to add something in the vein of scales. Perhaps even giving beats when that happens.<br /> <br /> So far i think i'll keep the merits and using the conditions for temporary gains.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? <br /> Is it feasible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:57:29-08:00","id":1011158,"title":"","content":"I personally use the &quot;keep the Merits and use Conditions to supplement,&quot; method. A character can have Resources to represent a reliable source of extra cash, or win the Lottery and get the Windfall Condition that they can resolve by spending a big sum on something.<br /> <br /> I think one of the big problems with moving completely over to Conditions is that (1) you pretty much have to have Persistent versions of some of them to make sense which just turns these things into Beat machines on top of the benefits they provide, and (2) you remove the Sanctity of Merits aspect of them.<br /> <br /> Now, for your group, those might not really matter, but in general it makes a big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:22:20-08:00","id":1011169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011158#post1011158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally use the &quot;keep the Merits and use Conditions to supplement,&quot; method. A character can have Resources to represent a reliable source of extra cash, or win the Lottery and get the Windfall Condition that they can resolve by spending a big sum on something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i dont want to change the merits my players have. So i will keep the merits<br /> Tho i didnt know there was a Windfall condition. Its pretty much what i was looking for. <br /> Where is it written? I have looked in the vampire corebook and its not there.<br /> <br /> Would there be something similar for the other merits? Like the player has gained a favor that he could resolve by 'spending' it ?<br /> <br /> As for the beats, i'd actually like for my players to have another way to earn them. They are new to the system and they're not earning as much beat per game as i expected (2 at the most each game). My guess is its still a bit counter intuitive for them to put themselves in negative circumstances to earn exp. So far none of them have changed a failure to a dramatic failure and they are very cautious about not being in situation that puts their humanity at risk. Also its my first 2nd ed game and I don't know the conditions sufficiently yet i think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:14:34-08:00","id":1011180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011169#post1011169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah i dont want to change the merits my players have. So i will keep the merits<br /> Tho i didnt know there was a Windfall condition. Its pretty much what i was looking for. <br /> Where is it written? I have looked in the vampire corebook and its not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such Condition in the books, but creating custom Conditions is something Storytellers are encouraged to do. I'm guessing Heavy either uses a custom Windfall Condition, or was just naming it as an example of a Condition that one could custom-make.<br /> <br /> Personally, I use the Cash Equipment for this purpose, but making it a Condition instead works if you want more sources of Beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011169#post1011169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there be something similar for the other merits? Like the player has gained a favor that he could resolve by 'spending' it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely something you could create as well. Or use Services.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011169#post1011169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the beats, i'd actually like for my players to have another way to earn them. They are new to the system and they're not earning as much beat per game as i expected (2 at the most each game). My guess is its still a bit counter intuitive for them to put themselves in negative circumstances to earn exp. So far none of them have changed a failure to a dramatic failure and they are very cautious about not being in situation that puts their humanity at risk. Also its my first 2nd ed game and I don't know the conditions sufficiently yet i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems pretty common for folks who are new to 2e. My first session running 2e, a player got the Spooked Condition (CofD core book), read it, gave me a quizzical look, and asked &quot;is there anything stopping me from just not Resolving this?&quot; I told her no, but if she didn't Resolve it she wouldn't get a Beat from it. The whole table gave an &quot;Ooooooh&quot; and from then on we never had any problems with reluctance to resolve Conditions or take dramatic failures. But I guess Iucked out, a lot of groups take more time to get used to the idea of accepting IC drawbacks in exchange for OOC rewards. And some folks just plain don't like that play style. Are you using Group Beats? I've heard a lot of STs have found that more successful, as it creates a perception that accepting negative effects from Conditions benefits the whole group, and a lot of players are more willing to take a hit for the team than to trade personal drawbacks for personal rewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:25:33-08:00","id":1011244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions#post1011140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Namely:<br /> - Retainer<br /> - Contact<br /> - Allies<br /> - Resource<br /> - Mentor<br /> - Status<br /> <br /> It occurred to me that the way i was using those merits fell more in line with conditions than the way they are written. By that i mean that if the player do something that would logically earn them the merit I don't bother with the exp spending. Also i've not been following the mechanics of these merits too closely, a player tells me what they want to accomplish and i judge if its feasible with the merits they have.<br /> I also really like the ... flowing nature of how conditions work, the way you gain and lose them.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of awarding the condition following appropriate story circumstances (same as any other condition). I'd also add something i call 'strings attached' which is what the players need to do in order to keep the condition.<br /> You earn beats for gaining or losing the condition.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to add something in the vein of scales. Perhaps even giving beats when that happens.<br /> <br /> So far i think i'll keep the merits and using the conditions for temporary gains.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> Is it feasible?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I do is just award them the merit dot as a &quot;temporary&quot; or gift. Like if a vampire creates a ghoul. I dont make them buy retainer or whatever applies to it better. I just &quot;gift&quot; it to them.<br /> <br /> Though until they actually spend the exp on the dots, I dont make it safe.<br /> <br /> Like a contact. They might find someone who helps them out and they keep going to that person over and over. I might just kill off that person if it helps my story or if they are abusing it (like a cop) I might have that person lose their job so they cant help anymore. Unless they spend the actual exp on it to make it &quot;safe&quot; If that makes any sense ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:46:13-08:00","id":1011317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011169#post1011169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tho i didnt know there was a Windfall condition. Its pretty much what i was looking for.<br /> Where is it written? I have looked in the vampire corebook and its not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, as guess, it's a personal custom Condition.<br /> <br /> I use it for things that are more abstract/complicated than just a pile of cash (in the form of Cash or Contraband equipment).<br /> <br /> The basic way I have it function it that the character can make a purchase as if they have Resources (or an appropriate other Merit) + 2, max. 5 for a single purchase of equipment or services that does not count towards the usual limitation of purchases with Merits.<br /> <br /> The Condition Resolves when that purchase is made, or the character's rating in a Merit that represents an economic asset (usual Resources, but also Merits like Safe Place) is increased with XP.<br /> <br /> The second half basically lets you use it as a discount on increasing those sorts of Merits if you want to &quot;invest&quot; instead of making a big purchase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would there be something similar for the other merits? </div> </div> </div>There are a few things already in the books. The Connected and Informed Conditions (CofD 2e core book) work well for a lot of the organization focused Merits you listed in your first post.<br /> <br /> A number of Conditions that could be put on NPCs could be used as well, but don't really seem necessary between Merits, and things like services. You don't need Retainer or a custom Condition to hire a limo driver for the night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the beats, i'd actually like for my players to have another way to earn them. They are new to the system and they're not earning as much beat per game as i expected (2 at the most each game). My guess is its still a bit counter intuitive for them to put themselves in negative circumstances to earn exp. So far none of them have changed a failure to a dramatic failure and they are very cautious about not being in situation that puts their humanity at risk. Also its my first 2nd ed game and I don't know the conditions sufficiently yet i think. </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that more Conditions doesn't really equate to more Beats. Cashing in a bunch of them at once isn't as good as spread them out more.<br /> <br /> To an extent, you've basically got to wait for something like what happened for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> when it finally clicks. Though something you can do to try to instigate this sooner rather than later are Conditions NPCs can put on the characters via Lashing Out, Disciplines, and even if you're worried about them feeling &quot;attacked&quot; have a friendly NPC use the Inspiring Merit on them.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that while Beats mostly come from negative situations, a lot of Beats also come from positive things. It's not &quot;have something bad happen to your character, take a Beat,&quot; it's, &quot;have something interesting happen to your character, take a Beat.&quot; Remembering to look at it from the perspective of having a given Beat opportunity stemming from something interesting makes it a lot easier to spurn player engagement with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T08:12:57-08:00","id":1012588,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the time it took to respond. Somehow I have less free time in the weekend than during the week. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1011140-changing-a-few-merits-into-positive-conditions?p=1011180#post1011180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you using Group Beats? I've heard a lot of STs have found that more successful, as it creates a perception that accepting negative effects from Conditions benefits the whole group, and a lot of players are more willing to take a hit for the team than to trade personal drawbacks for personal rewards.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be a moot point. I have one player who has 1 more beat but the rest of my players all have the same number of beats. <br /> <br /> Also, i am trying something different in that my players did not start as a coterie and i am trying to have them become a coterie through the story.<br /> Tho once that happens it may be a good idea to offer them the possibility of earning beats as a group. I'll give the matter some thought, thx.<br /> <br /> As for the conditions, you guys made me aware that i was coming at it from the wrong angle. Its not about unilaterally creating more opportunities for the players but making them more aware of the opportunities that is available to them. So i don't necessarily have to create anything but i have to concentrate on communicating more with my players i think.<br /> <br /> Anyway thanks for the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}